		id: 'verses-7-12',
		heading: `Verses 7-12: what trusting looks like next`,
		bodyHtml: `<p>The father does not leave trust abstract. He gives it three practical shapes. First, healing and refreshment for a person who stops trusting only in himself: &ldquo;This will bring healing to your body and refreshment to your bones.&rdquo; (Proverbs 3:8). Second, honoring our Father with what you have: &ldquo;Honor our Father with your wealth and with the firstfruits of all your produce.&rdquo; (Proverbs 3:9). Third, receiving correction as love: &ldquo;for our Father disciplines the one his heart loves, just as a father disciplines the son he delights in.&rdquo; (Proverbs 3:12).</p><p>The last one matters for anyone who has felt that a hard season meant our Father had left. The chapter says the opposite: the one he disciplines is the one his heart loves. The paths he makes straight are walked with a Father who delights in his child.`,
